: I know although I made this statement
Some of you may still not believe it, or you may say it won't happen again.
this will help to make the 8.0 version a smarter version, both in order to be able to work with more experienced people.
The 8.0 version is my most stable version, and I know it will affect your game stats a lot.
therefore, it will be a little more difficult to communicate with people
I had no problems with admins, and I think they did their job pretty well.
Before this release, the current admin list will be completely cleared, all bans will be removed, the warning of those who have been warned will be reset, but please don't do anything big by taking shelter of this.
and we need team for beta version, builders for map creation, testers to test and let us know
or admins who will memorize new commands and admins who have the ability to communicate with people, old admins can try again when this chance is removed
and a little note
new admins, builders/testers will not be deployed on main server until stable release of 8.0 in current version
they will take care of the other version in the learning and production phase
and the main subject of application
If you want to be an admin, tester, or builder, send the following email to buzreisiproductions@gmail.com
first set your topic, it can be like, #newadmin, #newbuilder, #newtester
then fill in the following information, is there a game you have taken part in before, have you been banned from any game, how are you in communicating/helping with people?
note, copy the information here, leave a space and add your own answer
Are you hasty or patient in memorizing something?
What would you do if a player asked you to teleport him to the same map as his friend?
what do you do if a player spammer
What would you do if a player spoke insultingly about a country?
Is there anything you did in any game, if there is, write down the game and what you did, note, it is not mandatory
What would you do if an admin mistreated a player and told you please don't tell develeporse it?
Thanks for participating!
